  "summary": {
    "as": "Passed Senate",
    "asOf": "2026-08-03",
    "date": "2026-08-26T21:47:56Z",
    "text": "Bankruptcy Threshold Adjustment Act of 2026\n\nThis bill restores changes that expired in 2024 applicable to debt limits for Subchapter V (small business reorganization) and Chapter 13 (the wage earner's plan) bankruptcies.\n\nSpecifically, the bill increases the debt limit under Subchapter\u00a0V from approximately $3.4 million to $7.5 million and increases the cumulative debt limit under Chapter 13 from approximately $2.1 million to $2.75 million.\n\nThe bill also applies both secured and unsecured debt towards the Chapter 13 limit. (Currently, separate limits apply to secured and unsecured debt under Chapter 13 bankruptcy.)"
  },
